WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Test 4. This is the IELTS listening test.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
You will hear a number of different recordings and you will have to answer questions on what you hear.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.000
There will be time for you to read the instructions and questions and you will have a chance to check your work.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
All the recordings will be played once only.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000
The test is in four parts.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:35.000
At the end of the test you will be given ten minutes to transfer your answers to an answer sheet.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Now turn to part one.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Part one. You will hear a supervisor in a supermarket talking to a new worker on her first day.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.000
First you have some time to look at questions one to six.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Now listen carefully and answer questions one to six.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Hello Charlotte. I'm Caden, one of the supervisors. Welcome to the team.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Hi Aidan.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.000
It's Caden.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.000
I'm so sorry.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Don't worry. People often get my name wrong. They never know how to spell it.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.000
It's K-A-E-D-E-N in case you ever need to write it.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.000
I'll try and remember.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:02.000
So there are a few practical things you need to sort out this morning.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Then I'll show you what you're going to do today.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:12.000
The email I received said to go to the front desk to show my letter of appointment and pick up my badge.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:18.000
You'll need that for the staff room and other areas of the supermarket where shoppers aren't allowed.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:23.000
So after you've finished at the front desk, I'll take you to the staff room.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:28.000
Put your coat and rucksack in one of the lockers there. Take whichever one is free.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Will I have a key?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:37.000
Yes. Try not to lose it. At the end of the day, leave it in the door for the next person to use.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.000
Will do.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:44.000
You also need to go to the HR department to see Tiffany. She's really helpful.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:50.000
I was told to bring my passport with me. HR need to take a note of the number in it?

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.000
That's right. Or you can show your ID card.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.000
I don't have one of those.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:02.000
OK. Tiffany will give you a uniform. They have lots in different sizes, so you just tell her what you need.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.000
I won't come with you to HR. I've got to go and sort something else out.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.000
Um, problem with a bread slicer.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.000
Is the HR office near the staff room?

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:18.000
The staff room's on the first floor and HR are a couple of floors above that, on the third floor.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.000
There's a staircase outside the staff room.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.000
OK.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.000
When you've finished with HR, come and find me in the bakery section of the shop.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.000
I'm looking forward to getting started.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:35.000
I'll just give you my phone number in case you can't find me. Have you got your phone there?

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:38.000
Yes. OK. Ready?

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:46.000
It's 0412 665903.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.000
OK. Done.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:58.000
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 7 to 10.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:22.000
Now listen and answer questions 7 to 10.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:34.000
So, Charlotte, your tasks today are in the bakery section, on the sushi counter and on the meat and fish counters.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.000
The first job is to check sell-by dates on the bread and cakes.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:43.000
If any of the dates are today's, put a new price label on the packaging.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:50.000
What if any of the labels are yesterday's dates or older? Do I throw those items away?

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:54.000
Yes, but that shouldn't happen. We check the stock every day.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:59.000
When something needs a new price label, put a yellow one on the package, next to the original price.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.000
OK.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.000
After that, you'll go to the sushi takeaway counter.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:08.000
Will I be preparing boxes of food?

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.000
For today, you'll just be helping the staff.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.000
Yes, of course.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:16.000
You'll see lots of flat cardboard boxes at one end of the counter.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:19.000
Beneath those is where we keep the plastic boxes.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:24.000
We run out of those really quickly, so you should bring more from the storeroom.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.000
Is that my only task on the sushi counter?

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:31.000
No, you also need to clean the area where they prepare the dishes.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.000
There are cloths and bottles of spray by the sink.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.000
Oh, and please make sure you clean that, too.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.000
Sure. That's important, isn't it?

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:42.000
Absolutely, but you mustn't wash up knives.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.000
You have to do some training before you're allowed to touch sharp objects.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.000
What should I do if there are any?

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.000
Ask someone to put them in the dishwasher.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:54.000
OK, thanks. I don't want to get anything wrong.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.000
Don't worry, you'll be fine. And I'll be around to help.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.000
Right.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.000
Finally, the meat and fish counters.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.000
You need to clean the area where staff serve customers,

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.000
including wiping the weighing scales.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:10.000
OK. Anything else?

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.000
The fish is laid on ice, but when that starts to melt,

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:16.000
you'll need to get more from the cold room.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.000
I know the staff on the food counters wear a hat.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.000
Will that be the same for me?

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.000
You won't be serving customers directly, so no.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:29.000
But make sure you put on thermal gloves when you take anything out of the cold room.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:33.000
The temperature's low enough in there to get frostbite from touching things.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.000
Understood.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.000
That is the end of part one.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.000
You now have one minute to check your answers to part one.

